This PR ensures that we always process epoll events with limited concurrency. Additionally, to avoid spinning the CPU in the event loop, we ensure that minimum `delay` is waited. This takes the processing time into consideration. Those changes produces very stable CPU times.

We should potentially expose EpollConfiguration to allow users to tweak the performance in more demanding environments.

